4. SCOPE — THIS IS A REDUCED EDITION

The Edition includes Core Foundation plus a single basic path through a
case (intake, financial-discovery intake, core drafting and
prefiling QC, case roadmap, and case closing). It does not include the
advanced discovery, mediation, GAL, research, contempt, name-change, prenup,
or trial systems, nor the customization or firm-adaptation tooling shipped
with a full suite license. A full suite license, purchased separately,
supersedes and extends this Edition.


5. NO LEGAL ADVICE — PROFESSIONAL RESPONSIBILITY REMAINS WITH THE MEMBER

THIS IS THE MOST IMPORTANT TERM IN THIS AGREEMENT.

The Edition is a drafting and workflow tool. It is not a lawyer, does not
practice law, and does not provide legal advice. Legal Authority Lab is not
engaged in the practice of law and forms no attorney-client relationship
with the Member or with any client of the Member.

The Member is solely responsible for:

  (a) the legal sufficiency, accuracy, and completeness of every document
      produced with the assistance of the Edition;
  (b) independently verifying every statute, rule, court decision, deadline,
      and procedural requirement before relying on it — the Edition marks
      authorities with a verification warning precisely because
      verification is the Member's duty and cannot be delegated to
      software;
  (c) confirming local judicial, division, circuit, county, and clerk
      practice, which changes without notice;
  (d) compliance with the Rules Regulating The Florida Bar, including the
      duties of competence, confidentiality, candor, supervision of
      nonlawyer assistance, and any applicable disclosure obligations
      concerning the use of artificial intelligence;
  (e) all attorney review and approval gates identified in the Edition.

No output of the Edition may be filed, served, or sent to a client, a court,
or an opposing party without review by a licensed Florida attorney.


